No it shouldn't. Wizard gets blessed +1 quarterstaff, +0 cloack of magic 
resistance, 1 wand, 2 rings, 3 potions, 3 scrolls, a spellbook of force 
bolt, an additonal spellbook, 20% chance for magic marker and 20% chance 
of blindfold in that order. No cursed items are generated in starting 
inventory.

Restrictions on random objects that can be generated into initial 
inventory are:

No wand of wishing, ring of levitation if elbereth is compiled in, 
potion of hallucination or acid, scrolls of amnesia, fire or blank 
paper, blank spellbook, ring of aggravate monster or hunger, a spellbook 
higher than level 3 or restricted to the class,monks don't get scrolls 
of enchant weapon nor wizards spellbook of force bolt (remember that 
these restrictions are for random initial items).

In addition there are four restricted items that cannot be randomly 
generated that are filled in during the item generation. They are all 
strenge objects initially but are filled this way:

If a wand, a ring or a potion of polymorph is generated the fist 
restricted item is ring of polymorph control.

If ring of polymorph control is created then first restricted item is
ring of polymorph, the second is spellbook of polymorph and third is 
potion of polymorph.

If a ring was generatated then fourth restricted is that ring type and 
same for spellbooks.

Remember that the code utilizes the order of item generation: wands are 
generated before rings.

